      "role": "user",
      "content": "those are good starting points for physical/infra factors, but we're looking for more granular community-level indicators. \n\nsometimes the variance we see seems tied to the social fabric of a neighborhood rather than just traffic or weather. when looking at high-density census tracts, what kind of sociological or community composition data might provide the most predictive power? i'm thinking about things that capture the 'character' of the area to help us refine the risk profiles for specific urban clusters.",
